From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 01:27:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Compile the matcher stack's assert-only frame count only when asserts are on

MatchStack::ExecuteInternal() keeps the frame count before a frame
runs in a local that only D_ASSERT() reads, so in a release build,
where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, -Wunused-variable reports it. The
guard keeps the local to the builds that assert; upstream later drops
the local with the assertion.

Carried here until the engine brings the same change.

---
 src/duckdb/src/parser/peg/matcher_stack.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/parser/peg/matcher_stack.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/parser/peg/matcher_stack.cpp
index 2b61728657..17519f9f0c 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/parser/peg/matcher_stack.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/parser/peg/matcher_stack.cpp
@@ -141,7 +141,9 @@ MatcherResult MatchStack::ExecuteInternal(const Matcher &matcher, MatchState &st
 	PushFrame(matcher, state);
 	while (!frames.empty()) {
 		auto &frame = *frames.back();
+#ifdef D_ASSERT_IS_ENABLED
 		auto frame_count = frames.size();
+#endif
 		ExecuteFrame(frame);
 		if (!frame.HasResult()) {
 			D_ASSERT(frames.size() > frame_count);
